# Blank Panel — UI structure

Minimal cabinet shell; no blocks/widgets staging.

```
internal/ui/
  layout/       # shell, header, sidebar, helpers — permanent app chrome
  components/   # dumb reusable pieces (icon, toggles, account menu)
internal/views/
  *.templ       # route pages (login, dashboard, …)
  partials/     # shell head assets, header trailing glue
  models.go     # LayoutData, LoginPageData, …
internal/fixtures/
  locale/*.json # i18n copy
```

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `internal/ui/layout` | Sidebar, mobile sheet, header, theme toggle hooks |
| `internal/ui/components` | Props-only UI; no HTTP, auth, or fetch |
| `internal/views` | Compose layout + resolved fixture strings |
| `internal/cabinet` | Routes, auth gate, locale + asset wiring |

**views** receive resolved strings/structs only — no `fixtures.LoadLocale` inside `.templ`.

When adding a cabinet page: extend `paneldef`, add handler in `cabinet/feature.go`, add `internal/views/<page>.templ`, extend `fixtures.Locale` + every `locale/*.json`, update `@source` in `web/static/css/input.css` if new paths.
